config IO
	bool "io: byte stream reader and writer interfaces"
	default y
	select STATUS
	help
	  The el_reader and el_writer interfaces, helpers built on them, a
	  reader over caller-provided memory, the el_buf memory buffer and
	  the writer that ends in one, a buffered writer, and the contract
	  test suite for backends. Freestanding: needs only memcpy() and
	  memmove().

config IO_POSIX
	bool "io_posix: POSIX file descriptor backend"
	default y
	depends on IO && PLATFORM_POSIX
	help
	  Reader and writer over a file descriptor the caller owns, using
	  read(2) and write(2). Available only when the toolchain provides
	  <unistd.h>.

config IO_ALLOC
	bool "io_alloc: buffer storage that grows, over an allocator"
	default y
	depends on IO && ALLOC
	help
	  el_grow_buf: an el_buf whose storage comes from an el_allocator
	  and grows as needed, for a message or a burst of unknown size. It
	  is the one part of io that needs alloc: turn it off and io builds
	  and links no allocator. Freestanding: needs memcpy().

config IO_ZEPHYR_UART
	bool "io_zephyr_uart: a Zephyr UART as a writer"
	default y
	depends on IO && PLATFORM_ZEPHYR_UART
	help
	  el_zephyr_uart_poll, a writer that passes each byte to
	  uart_poll_out(). Available in a Zephyr build whose configuration
	  has CONFIG_SERIAL; interrupt-driven mode is not needed. Receiving
	  on a UART is ring's RING_ZEPHYR_UART.
